      "summary": "Endometriosis can cause severe period pain, pelvic pain, pain with sex, and fertility issues. NHS: see a GP if periods disrupt life; diagnosis may involve specialist pathways. Emergency: sudden severe one-sided pelvic pain, fainting, or heavy bleeding (consider ectopic/other acute causes — see related entries). Never invent hormone or pain-drug doses.",
